  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "ATM-QA-016" ;
  triage:title "Phase AU status headers stale (\"PLANNING ACTIVE\"/\"proposed\") despite AU.1-AU.3 being verifiably complete" ;
  triage:description "req-qa's RELPREP-QA-R1 re-run (PR #1068, chore/changelog-1.4.4) found docs/project-plan.md section 53 still headers Phase AU as '[PLANNING ACTIVE]' and docs/plans/phase-au/plan-phase-au.md still carries top-level 'status: proposed', even though all three AU sprint docs (AU.1, AU.2, AU.3) show status: complete, the AU.3 sibling write module exists in code (crates/atm-core/src/write/{mod.rs,pipeline.rs,acknowledgement.rs}), and both AU2 triage findings (AU2-RBQA-F001, AU2-QA-VISITOR-CYCLE-001) are closed/fixed. CHANGELOG.md's 1.4.4 entry correctly asserts Phase AU shipped, creating a cross-document conflict with the two stale status headers. Documentation-only gap; no code/behavior defect. Independently verified by quality-mgr at docs/project-plan.md:1482 and docs/plans/phase-au/plan-phase-au.md:3 on the synced tree (commit 18e0dca2d)." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-at" ;
